EqzLfpUf", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21611, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016iHz2UVLrUSjB7EqzLfpUf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 26217, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018LSkCYobedbZZmTW9JJrcd", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy, seq 3) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 0.18. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway through (orchestrator error after us-east), leaving the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56817, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018LSkCYobedbZZmTW9JJrcd", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56817, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018LSkCYobedbZZmTW9JJrcd", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58951, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JY9NqWQNrxni3StjL2PMpP", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59251, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JY9NqWQNrxni3StjL2PMpP", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59251, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JY9NqWQNrxni3StjL2PMpP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64079, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. I've opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** All three regions (us-east, us-west and eu-west) were running v2.3.1, the latest deploy. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback to v2.3.0 stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving the regions on different versions. I tried once more and it finished in all regions. Checking afterwards, the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't open a second one and page on-call twice. The incident describes the failure, the stalled first rollback, the current state and these follow-ups:\n   - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it. It has never been healthy in production, so redeploying it would need change-manager approval.\n   - Look into why the deployment system halted the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ri6q8G9jYrFEGSFWTxjjmX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_n